WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.820
What is slippage?

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:15.080
In DeFi, slippage happens when the final price of your trade is different from what you expected.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:19.000
This can be for a variety of reasons, all of which relate to the underlying mechanics

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.120
of blockchain technology.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:25.400
Why it happens

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.440
Slippage is driven by three main factors.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.840
Low liquidity, high volatility and network congestion.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:38.520
In short, if your trade is too big or the market moves too fast, prices may shift before final

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.600
transaction confirmation.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.920
How to reduce slippage?

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.200
You can't eliminate slippage, but you can manage it.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:53.840
Use low slippage tolerance, trade in deep pools and avoid volatile times.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.340
Tools for smart trading.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:01.240
Some platforms offer limit orders, slippage warnings and real-time previews.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:07.320
Layer twos and dynamic AMMs also help reduce execution delays.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.640
Slippage as strategy.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.640
Advanced traders use slippage for arbitrage or laddering orders.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.720
If used well, it can be a tool, not just a risk.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.920
Know the gap.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:28.040
Slippage is part of every DeFi trade. Mastering it means smarter execution, less risk and

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:28.960
better outcomes.
